  "executive_briefing": "The 2026 global tax landscape is defined by the rigid consolidation of the OECD Pillar Two 15% minimum tax, which is now moving from conceptual framework to active enforcement and active reporting via publications like the 2026 OECD Corporate Tax Statistics. Nations, particularly in the ASEAN region such as Singapore with its MMT Act and 17% headline corporate rate, are recalibrating their corporate tax incentives to maintain FDI appeal while adhering to global standards. Simultaneously, digital tax administration and continuous transaction controls are accelerating via mandatory e-invoicing rollouts like Singapore's phased GST InvoiceNow. Geopolitical trade volatility remains a persistent feature, as major economies continue to navigate tariff disputes and legal challenges over unilateral economic strategies.",
